WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.475
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.745 --> 00:09.025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

3
01:49.745 --> 01:50.785
Morning.

4
01:52.465 --> 01:54.665
I need to talk to you.

5
01:58.505 --> 02:01.225
They said you rushed out suddenly yesterday.

6
02:01.825 --> 02:04.505
I didn't dare call you, and you went quiet.

7
02:04.585 --> 02:05.425
So,

8
02:06.505 --> 02:08.304
this morning, when I ran into Zhao Heng,

9
02:08.385 --> 02:10.385
I asked him how you were doing.

10
02:11.185 --> 02:12.585
Why didn't you dare call me?

11
02:12.665 --> 02:14.185
I was afraid you'd misinterpret it.

12
02:14.785 --> 02:16.985
I should've told you before I joined

13
02:17.065 --> 02:18.785
the Celestial Insurance project team.

14
02:19.425 --> 02:21.825
But I worried things wouldn't come across clearly over a call,

15
02:21.905 --> 02:23.305
so I wanted to talk to you in person.

16
02:24.825 --> 02:27.385
Turns out Ma Ke told you already.

17
02:30.185 --> 02:31.425
I wouldn't misinterpret it.

18
02:31.505 --> 02:33.465
It's not my personal project.

19
02:34.705 --> 02:36.505
Don't talk to me like that.

20
02:37.585 --> 02:38.665
So let's talk work.

21
02:38.745 --> 02:40.705
Ma Ke asked me to help you get up to speed on the project.

22
02:42.585 --> 02:43.985
You know my family situation.

23
02:44.585 --> 02:45.585
My dad keeps assuming

24
02:45.665 --> 02:48.465
I landed the Ande Energy project only because of his connections.

25
02:49.225 --> 02:52.025
That day, when you said right here

26
02:52.545 --> 02:55.065
that digital finance was the next big trend,

27
02:55.145 --> 02:56.665
I wanted to give it a shot too.

28
02:56.745 --> 02:59.865
Unexpectedly, Mr. Pi assigned me to the Celestial Insurance project team.

29
02:59.945 --> 03:03.105
He said since we get along well, we'd make good partners.

30
03:04.185 --> 03:05.345
So,

31
03:05.865 --> 03:08.625
I never meant to steal your project.

32
03:09.945 --> 03:11.625
Still, you didn't turn it down.

33
03:12.625 --> 03:14.145
True. I didn't.

34
03:14.225 --> 03:17.145
Because I saw it as a chance to compete with you fairly.

35
03:17.225 --> 03:18.345
I didn't want to give up.

36
03:19.345 --> 03:21.305
I want to prove my ability

37
03:21.385 --> 03:22.745
to my dad through this.

38
03:24.025 --> 03:24.865
You're right.

39
03:24.945 --> 03:26.785
As I switched projects midway,

40
03:26.865 --> 03:28.985
there's no reason you can't join in halfway.

41
03:30.665 --> 03:31.985
You're not mad anymore?

42
03:33.665 --> 03:35.625
It's no big deal.

43
03:35.705 --> 03:37.825
After those sarcastic remarks I made, I let it go.

44
03:39.665 --> 03:41.865
Then friendship first, competition second.

45
04:33.145 --> 04:34.185
Finally wrapped it up.

46
04:35.985 --> 04:37.825
Come on, let's grab something to eat.

47
04:37.905 --> 04:38.865
All done?

48
04:39.505 --> 04:42.145
I'm passing. I've got a gym appointment at 9:30 p.m.

49
04:42.745 --> 04:44.145
I mean that poser.

50
04:44.745 --> 04:47.305
After we cleared the air, I can be genuine friends with him.

51
04:47.385 --> 04:48.585
That's great.

52
04:48.665 --> 04:49.505
Eat more,

53
04:50.185 --> 04:51.505
but don't put on weight.

54
04:55.945 --> 04:58.785
Fine, don't eat then. I can eat alone.

55
05:00.345 --> 05:01.225
Boss, just one.

56
05:01.305 --> 05:02.945
One bowl of beef noodles.

57
05:06.825 --> 05:10.145
If my presence here bothers you, I can leave right away.

58
05:10.225 --> 05:11.545
I don't own this place.

59
05:16.585 --> 05:18.865
Right. One alcohol-free beer, too.

60
05:18.945 --> 05:20.025
Okay.

61
05:22.585 --> 05:25.225
What's wrong? In a bad mood?

62
05:26.345 --> 05:27.185
No.

63
05:29.585 --> 05:30.905
Oh, thanks.

64
05:41.105 --> 05:42.625
Why aren't you prying any further this time?

65
05:44.505 --> 05:45.665
I'm done asking.

66
05:45.745 --> 05:47.305
Don't want you to think I'm always pestering you.

67
05:47.385 --> 05:49.185
I invited Xu Chi out for dinner,

68
05:49.265 --> 05:50.585
and she said she was hitting the gym.

69
05:50.665 --> 05:53.305
But I just saw her heading home, not to the gym.

70
05:54.265 --> 05:55.225
You…

71
05:55.745 --> 05:58.345
I think she means jogging with Ye Xinzhi.

72
05:58.425 --> 06:00.825
They're neighbors. It makes sense that they go the same way.

73
06:01.865 --> 06:03.385
How do you know that?

74
06:03.465 --> 06:04.385
I…

75
06:05.105 --> 06:06.665
I saw them jogging in the morning.

76
06:06.745 --> 06:09.305
But I just feel like something's wrong.

77
06:09.385 --> 06:11.265
What's wrong?

78
06:11.345 --> 06:13.345
Xu Chi and I are on the same project team now.

79
06:13.425 --> 06:15.665
Logically, we work together more than before.

80
06:15.745 --> 06:18.865
She cooperates and shares everything with me as she should, flawlessly.

81
06:18.945 --> 06:19.945
But…

82
06:22.745 --> 06:24.065
For example, just now,

83
06:24.145 --> 06:25.545
I invited her to dinner, and she turned me down,

84
06:25.625 --> 06:28.825
telling me when, where, and with whom in full detail.

85
06:28.905 --> 06:30.745
Yet I feel like something's wrong.

86
06:31.385 --> 06:32.705
Super business-like, huh?

87
06:35.705 --> 06:36.585
Ms. Bu,

88
06:36.665 --> 06:39.905
it's my great honor to sit and talk with you.

89
06:39.985 --> 06:41.665
I hope I can play the host

90
06:41.745 --> 06:43.865
for you sometime in the future.

91
06:44.545 --> 06:45.385
She sounds like this, right?

92
06:46.465 --> 06:47.305
Why would she act like that?

93
06:47.985 --> 06:49.545
There's nothing strange in this.

94
06:49.625 --> 06:51.745
Since you don't treat her as a friend, why would she treat you as one?

95
06:51.825 --> 06:53.545
That's nonsense! When

96
06:54.065 --> 06:56.105
haven't I treated her as a friend?

97
06:59.385 --> 07:02.025
The way you're acting now can easily send the wrong signal.

98
07:03.465 --> 07:06.305
Before joining the team, I laid out every detail

99
07:06.385 --> 07:08.585
and background to her clearly.

100
07:08.665 --> 07:09.785
So you mean

101
07:09.865 --> 07:12.065
once you explained everything to her,

102
07:12.145 --> 07:14.585
she has to accept it all, right?

103
07:14.665 --> 07:16.585
Think you're some rich young lady?

104
07:17.625 --> 07:20.025
Wait. You actually are one.

105
07:26.825 --> 07:27.945
What are you doing?

106
07:28.585 --> 07:29.785
Are you really going to confront her?

107
07:29.865 --> 07:31.545
I need to figure out why.

108
07:31.625 --> 07:33.945
She is my only friend. I can't hold it in. Give it back to me.

109
07:34.025 --> 07:35.305
You want the truth?

110
07:35.385 --> 07:36.505
I'll tell you.

111
07:37.105 --> 07:38.265
You've got low EQ.

112
07:38.865 --> 07:39.865
What did you say?

113
07:39.945 --> 07:42.305
-Say that again. -Is what I said wrong?

114
07:43.385 --> 07:44.705
Look at how you act.

115
07:45.225 --> 07:47.225
You hold your head high, all proud, like a swan,

116
07:47.305 --> 07:48.865
and you blow up over the smallest problem.

117
07:48.945 --> 07:50.545
That's low EQ.

118
07:51.145 --> 07:53.185
No wonder your dad has grown to dislike you over the years.

119
07:54.105 --> 07:56.185
You love Zhang's Crispy Pastries,

120
07:56.265 --> 07:57.705
and this little brat knocked them all over.

121
07:57.785 --> 07:59.505
What little brat?

122
07:59.585 --> 08:01.105
That's your brother.

123
08:01.185 --> 08:02.785
Do you even act like an older sister?

124
08:03.305 --> 08:05.185
Bad Tianna! Bad Tianna!

125
08:05.265 --> 08:06.665
No wonder after over two decades, you've got no real friends

126
08:06.745 --> 08:08.305
except Xu Chi.

127
08:14.665 --> 08:15.505
Go on.

128
08:16.105 --> 08:17.705
You call her your best friend, right?

129
08:18.665 --> 08:20.545
She knows you live at Bairui Apartments.

130
08:20.625 --> 08:22.985
She knows your life goal is to earn your dad's approval

131
08:23.065 --> 08:24.585
and take over Siwei Group.

132
08:24.665 --> 08:26.105
When you're upset,

133
08:26.185 --> 08:28.225
she drops all her work and stays up late drinking with you.

134
08:28.305 --> 08:30.905
But what about you? Do you know where she lives?

135
08:31.905 --> 08:33.985
Do you know what her life goal is?

136
08:34.065 --> 08:35.784
Where were you when she was upset?

137
08:36.545 --> 08:38.185
She stays at the 9 Days Inn over there.

138
08:38.264 --> 08:39.985
A place of just over 20 square meters.

139
08:40.065 --> 08:41.105
Why did she join Maxmise?

140
08:41.185 --> 08:43.865
To earn more money to buy back her mother's old apartment.

141
08:43.945 --> 08:46.385
The down payment is over a million. That's exactly what your car cost.

142
08:50.505 --> 08:51.905
How do you know that?

143
08:53.425 --> 08:54.305
Did she tell you?

144
08:54.385 --> 08:55.745
She didn't.

145
08:58.065 --> 08:59.185
At her workstation

146
09:00.145 --> 09:02.585
is the real estate flyer for that old apartment.

147
09:03.225 --> 09:04.425
Feels like

148
09:05.585 --> 09:06.865
even I, her regular colleague,

149
09:06.945 --> 09:09.025
know more about her than you,

150
09:09.665 --> 09:11.385
her supposed bestie.

151
09:26.385 --> 09:28.225
I only got this car the day before yesterday.

152
09:28.305 --> 09:29.625
You memorized my license plate so soon?

153
09:30.985 --> 09:32.785
Didn't you say you were broke?

154
09:33.465 --> 09:35.585
-Then why buy a car? -Easy there.

155
09:35.665 --> 09:37.985
Every man needs his own car.

156
09:38.065 --> 09:39.705
Mine is a used car.

157
09:40.825 --> 09:43.385
Sure, I came from a poor family,

158
09:43.465 --> 09:44.945
but I get by fine now.

159
09:45.025 --> 09:47.185
After all, Maxmise pays pretty well.

160
09:48.385 --> 09:51.345
So, you actually care about me.

161
09:52.625 --> 09:55.385
I don't care about you. Why are you following me?

162
09:56.665 --> 09:58.225
To make sure you get home safe.

163
09:58.305 --> 10:00.265
You're in a bad mood, and it's late at night.

164
10:00.345 --> 10:03.385
If anything dangerous happens on the way, I can rush over and play hero.

165
10:03.465 --> 10:05.145
Nothing bad happening

166
10:05.225 --> 10:06.345
would be ideal.

167
10:06.425 --> 10:08.185
But you'd notice me quietly

168
10:08.265 --> 10:10.265
watching over you from behind.

169
10:10.865 --> 10:13.145
Maybe you'd be touched and give me a chance.

170
10:16.425 --> 10:17.705
You're being awfully blunt.

171
10:17.785 --> 10:19.265
Haven't I always been

172
10:19.785 --> 10:21.225
a true rogue in your eyes?

173
10:22.505 --> 10:24.545
I know exactly what you're thinking.

174
10:25.145 --> 10:26.225
You're thinking that money

175
10:26.305 --> 10:28.185
would be enough to turn your whole family's fortunes

176
10:28.265 --> 10:29.585
around, aren't you?

177
10:29.665 --> 10:32.945
I don't have that much value to offer, so wake up!

178
10:39.225 --> 10:40.985
Go on. I'm giving you a chance.

179
10:41.945 --> 10:44.105
No. My beat-up car

180
10:44.185 --> 10:47.745
is way too shabby for anything adult-rated.

181
10:48.745 --> 10:50.705
How about we go somewhere else?

182
10:57.585 --> 10:58.785
You don't have the guts.

183
10:59.705 --> 11:02.065
With all that tough talk just now,

184
11:02.625 --> 11:04.145
you were trying

185
11:04.225 --> 11:07.785
to get my attention, just like before, right?

186
11:07.865 --> 11:09.345
I won't buy

187
11:09.865 --> 11:11.385
a single word of it.

188
11:11.465 --> 11:13.105
Xu Chi is nothing like you.

189
11:34.265 --> 11:37.185
Never say that men have no guts.

190
11:37.265 --> 11:39.225
Believe it or not, I could do something right now.

191
11:41.985 --> 11:44.665
I don't. Yes.

192
11:44.745 --> 11:45.785
And one more thing.

193
11:47.065 --> 11:48.505
In my car,

194
11:49.865 --> 11:51.265
don't say anyone else's name,

195
11:52.505 --> 11:53.745
male or female,

196
11:54.345 --> 11:55.265
or I'll get jealous.

197
12:03.945 --> 12:04.785
Alright.

198
12:04.865 --> 12:07.185
Fasten your seatbelt. I'll drive you home and then leave.

199
12:09.225 --> 12:10.265
Okay.

200
12:14.305 --> 12:15.145
Wait.

201
12:18.825 --> 12:20.665
Am I really that terrible as a person?

202
12:22.185 --> 12:23.505
Not exactly terrible.

203
12:24.545 --> 12:26.185
You're used to being on top,

204
12:26.265 --> 12:27.705
so you don't know how to get along with people like us.

205
12:28.865 --> 12:29.865
People like you?

206
12:30.505 --> 12:31.345
Yeah.

207
12:31.865 --> 12:33.585
Ordinary folks like Xu Chi and me.

208
12:34.465 --> 12:36.785
I grew up from a village to a small town.

209
12:37.585 --> 12:38.745
She's half-orphaned.

210
12:39.465 --> 12:40.505
On the surface,

211
12:40.585 --> 12:42.305
we look polished, working in the CBD,

212
12:42.385 --> 12:44.305
earning decent salaries.

213
12:45.185 --> 12:47.465
But the truth is, we have to grind for over a decade

214
12:47.545 --> 12:50.385
to reach the starting line you were born into.

215
12:50.465 --> 12:53.145
Take switching project teams, for example.

216
12:53.225 --> 12:54.945
She has to get Sha Sha's approval,

217
12:55.625 --> 12:58.505
yet you made requests to the partner directly.

218
12:59.825 --> 13:01.025
No.

219
13:01.105 --> 13:03.505
But Xu Chi told me she is confident

220
13:03.585 --> 13:05.945
and doesn't care about my resource advantages.

221
13:06.025 --> 13:07.785
As I switch projects midway,

222
13:07.865 --> 13:09.985
there's no reason you can't join in halfway.

223
13:10.785 --> 13:13.065
And we both compete on our own merits.

224
13:13.145 --> 13:15.705
I want to see through this opportunity

225
13:15.785 --> 13:17.865
which one of us will be Maxmise's Rookie of the Year.

226
13:18.945 --> 13:21.105
At your age, you still buy into this?

227
13:21.705 --> 13:22.705
Young lady,

228
13:23.705 --> 13:26.705
whether in friendship or romance,

229
13:26.785 --> 13:28.585
a disparity in roots makes for a bitter struggle.

230
13:32.305 --> 13:33.665
We grind for over a decade

231
13:33.745 --> 13:35.705
just not to envy your background.

232
13:36.225 --> 13:38.105
But that doesn't mean we won't admire it.

233
13:39.385 --> 13:41.945
Regardless of your bad temper or low EQ day-to-day,

234
13:42.025 --> 13:44.745
once you cross someone's bottom line, there will be no turning back.

235
13:46.985 --> 13:48.785
What bottom line of Xu Chi did I cross?

236
13:50.145 --> 13:51.705
Did I steal her resources

237
13:51.785 --> 13:54.425
or go to Mr. Pi directly for materials?

238
13:54.505 --> 13:58.025
Stealing resources is trivial.

239
13:58.105 --> 14:01.225
If it were me, there's one thing that would break my heart.

240
14:01.865 --> 14:03.505
You never gave her a heads-up

241
14:03.585 --> 14:05.345
before you acted.

242
14:05.425 --> 14:06.905
-I have to hang up. -Wait.

243
14:06.985 --> 14:07.745
What is it?

244
14:09.345 --> 14:11.625
Never mind. I'll tell you some other time.

245
14:13.945 --> 14:15.065
It's not that you forgot.

246
14:15.945 --> 14:17.305
You never thought about it.

247
14:17.985 --> 14:19.545
It's not that you don't trust her.

248
14:19.625 --> 14:22.025
Subconsciously, you never took her into account.

249
14:23.505 --> 14:25.985
That's what I meant, the saddest part from the start.

250
14:28.385 --> 14:29.585
You never saw her as a friend.

251
14:38.305 --> 14:39.705
Fine, then there's no turning back.

252
14:44.585 --> 14:45.425
Are you leaving?

253
14:46.825 --> 14:49.785
Someone as thin-skinned as her doesn't deserve to be my friend.

254
14:55.185 --> 14:56.225
Don't follow me.

255
15:26.425 --> 15:27.345
What are you grinning at?

256
15:33.785 --> 15:34.665
Yesterday…

257
15:34.745 --> 15:35.945
Xu Chi,

258
15:36.545 --> 15:38.385
why are you

259
15:38.465 --> 15:39.865
being so fake-polite with me?

260
15:40.985 --> 15:42.065
Right.

261
15:42.145 --> 15:43.425
Chi.

262
15:43.505 --> 15:44.785
Argue with her like this later.

263
15:47.105 --> 15:48.105
Tell her…

264
16:02.705 --> 16:05.465
Today I'm here to apologize to you for the second time.

265
16:06.225 --> 16:07.425
A,

266
16:07.505 --> 16:10.105
I didn't consult you before asking to join this project.

267
16:10.185 --> 16:11.145
B,

268
16:11.665 --> 16:14.425
I never looked into the root cause of why you've been upset for so long.

269
16:14.505 --> 16:15.385
That's my fault.

270
16:17.225 --> 16:18.465
-You don't have to-- -Don't speak yet.

271
16:19.065 --> 16:21.145
Other than these, I don't believe

272
16:21.225 --> 16:22.945
I've done anything wrong to you.

273
16:23.545 --> 16:25.465
Why didn't you tell me you were upset?

274
16:25.545 --> 16:28.105
Even if I acted improperly,

275
16:28.185 --> 16:30.945
that's no excuse for you to be fake-polite with me.

276
16:31.025 --> 16:32.105
Fine.

277
16:32.185 --> 16:33.625
Zhao Heng said I don't care about you.

278
16:34.425 --> 16:36.505
But you've never opened up to me, either.

279
16:36.585 --> 16:39.265
That's just how I am. If you don't want to tell me, I won't ask.

280
16:39.345 --> 16:41.745
I'm giving you space. Is that so wrong?

281
16:48.545 --> 16:49.385
-Tianna-- -Don't come closer.

282
16:51.705 --> 16:53.305
Moved to hear me apologize?

283
16:55.745 --> 16:57.225
I could've done what you do,

284
16:57.745 --> 17:00.305
taking advantage of your emotions, pretending to make up with you,

285
17:00.385 --> 17:02.905
and keeping on being your polite bestie.

286
17:03.585 --> 17:04.585
But I can't.

287
17:04.665 --> 17:07.105
There's a thorn in my heart, and I can't remove it.

288
17:07.184 --> 17:09.785
What I want is a friend

289
17:09.865 --> 17:11.545
with full mutual trust.

290
17:11.625 --> 17:12.665
I thought you were different from everyone else.

291
17:12.745 --> 17:14.105
Then what are you doing here?

292
17:14.184 --> 17:15.905
What… What am I doing here?

293
17:15.985 --> 17:17.665
I'm here to tell you

294
17:17.745 --> 17:19.825
that from now on, in the Celestial Insurance project,

295
17:19.905 --> 17:21.464
I will hold nothing back.

296
17:22.105 --> 17:23.665
I'll prove I'm better

297
17:25.065 --> 17:26.825
than you with real results.

298
17:27.985 --> 17:29.585
Do you think

299
17:29.665 --> 17:31.105
she acted like a kid in kindergarten?

300
17:31.185 --> 17:34.145
When upset, she comes right up and says she will not play with me anymore.

301
17:35.705 --> 17:37.305
Actually, it was good advice

302
17:37.385 --> 17:39.225
when you told me that day to talk things out with her.

303
17:39.305 --> 17:43.465
I used to see her as this aloof, strong leading lady,

304
17:43.545 --> 17:46.265
so I was trying too hard in front of her.

305
17:46.865 --> 17:50.225
Now I realize she's just a kitten hissing and showing its claws.

306
17:51.545 --> 17:52.625
So you teased her on purpose?

307
17:52.705 --> 17:53.945
Yeah.

308
17:54.865 --> 17:56.145
But you've always outshone me.

309
17:58.345 --> 18:01.705
Come to think of it, we're not actually that close.

310
18:01.785 --> 18:03.585
We've only been coworkers for six months.

311
18:03.665 --> 18:07.385
I did help you once when you were down,

312
18:07.465 --> 18:09.105
but our friendship amounts to just a bottle of drinks.

313
18:10.145 --> 18:11.865
You've always had no friends,

314
18:11.945 --> 18:13.585
so out of gratitude,

315
18:13.665 --> 18:16.745
you projected all your ideal hopes for friendship onto me.

316
18:17.545 --> 18:19.985
You're right. I really

317
18:20.065 --> 18:20.945
don't deserve to be your friend.

318
18:21.785 --> 18:24.225
Hiding my inferiority complex around you has been exhausting.

319
18:24.305 --> 18:26.305
So bring on the rivalry.

320
18:26.385 --> 18:28.665
Let's reset everything. Be just colleagues

321
18:29.265 --> 18:31.945
and compete all out, so we'll have no hard feelings.

322
18:32.025 --> 18:33.225
What do you say?

323
18:34.305 --> 18:35.865
What do I say?

324
18:36.625 --> 18:37.465
Fine.

325
18:39.185 --> 18:41.025
I'll hold nothing back from now on.

326
18:41.105 --> 18:42.705
I'll

327
18:43.345 --> 18:45.025
-hold, hold… -Hold nothing back!

328
18:48.225 --> 18:49.505
So annoying.

329
18:51.665 --> 18:53.265
She has issued her challenge.

330
18:53.345 --> 18:56.385
If I don't take her challenge head-on, she'll think I'm dismissing her anger,

331
18:56.465 --> 18:57.505
and she'll fly into another fit of rage.

332
18:57.585 --> 19:00.625
So letting her punch at thin air like this

333
19:00.705 --> 19:01.745
is way more fun, right?

334
19:02.585 --> 19:04.745
Aren't you afraid of losing to her?

335
19:05.745 --> 19:08.025
My confidence has long been fully restored.

336
19:08.105 --> 19:10.625
After all, I have to live up to all your bitter advice.

337
19:11.545 --> 19:15.105
Besides, the Celestial Insurance project is managed by Ma Ke.

338
19:15.185 --> 19:17.625
Both Bu Tianna and I are junior analysts brought in halfway.

339
19:17.705 --> 19:20.225
Even if we go at it

340
19:20.305 --> 19:22.385
and polish our proposals to perfection,

341
19:22.465 --> 19:24.705
the winner of our little competition won't be promoted

342
19:24.785 --> 19:26.745
to consulting manager, right?

343
19:34.905 --> 19:36.705
It's such a relief to clear the air with you.

344
19:36.785 --> 19:39.545
No more working out of the café.

345
19:39.625 --> 19:40.865
I can take a breather

346
19:40.945 --> 19:43.105
and enjoy this amazing view.

347
19:43.185 --> 19:45.665
No need to worry about running into Maxmise colleagues out in public.

348
19:45.745 --> 19:46.905
This is really nice.

349
20:18.465 --> 20:20.665
By the way, Du will be here soon.

350
20:20.745 --> 20:23.505
How's the data analysis for Benyuan Digital Collectibles coming?

351
20:28.705 --> 20:30.945
All documents have been sent, except for one file.

352
20:32.745 --> 20:33.865
Can I ask a question out of curiosity?

353
20:34.665 --> 20:35.665
Are you and Du

354
20:35.745 --> 20:38.465
planning to muscle in on the partnership between Wen Ruosen

355
20:38.545 --> 20:39.425
and Benyuan Digital Collectibles?

356
20:42.425 --> 20:43.345
What makes you say that?

357
20:44.865 --> 20:46.945
The documents you had me compile are extremely detailed.

358
20:47.665 --> 20:48.625
You also asked me to draft

359
20:48.705 --> 20:50.625
an investment prospectus for the digital collectible gallery,

360
20:51.305 --> 20:53.665
run data simulations, and conduct research.

361
20:53.745 --> 20:55.265
Only competitors

362
20:55.345 --> 20:57.265
would dig into another firm's business thoroughly.

363
20:59.705 --> 21:01.105
Quite the opposite.

364
21:01.185 --> 21:03.585
Our goal is to make this partnership happen.

365
21:06.945 --> 21:08.105
Alright.

366
21:09.225 --> 21:11.265
I'd better work on the documents in the hotel,

367
21:11.345 --> 21:12.785
so I won't get in your and Du's way.

368
21:13.425 --> 21:14.385
Aren't you going to ask why?

369
21:15.265 --> 21:16.825
You'll tell me when you're ready.

370
21:24.985 --> 21:28.305
Could you check your phone? Just check your--

371
21:33.145 --> 21:34.225
Ms. Xu is here too.

372
21:34.305 --> 21:37.785
If you had told me she was here, I wouldn't have parked so fast.

373
21:37.865 --> 21:38.905
I could've driven around a bit longer.

374
21:38.985 --> 21:41.185
No, it's fine. I'm leaving now. I won't hold up your meeting.

375
21:41.265 --> 21:43.305
I'll send you the data in about half an hour.

376
21:43.385 --> 21:44.225
-See you. -Off I go.

377
21:44.305 --> 21:46.025
Wait, don't go. Come back.

378
21:47.025 --> 21:47.865
What data?

379
21:50.665 --> 21:52.025
Ye, what's wrong with you?

380
21:53.385 --> 21:55.185
Look how hot it is outside.

381
21:55.265 --> 21:56.945
You're sending her out to work on data.

382
21:57.025 --> 21:58.345
Have you got any decency?

383
21:58.425 --> 21:59.705
-I'm fine. -No, no need.

384
21:59.785 --> 22:01.465
You stay here and work. Alright?

385
22:01.545 --> 22:03.985
We can talk right here. It's nothing urgent.

386
22:04.065 --> 22:05.705
You won't be a bother. You work here.

387
22:05.785 --> 22:07.505
That's settled.

388
22:11.345 --> 22:12.785
It's quiet here. You can work here.

389
22:13.505 --> 22:14.345
Okay.

390
22:41.945 --> 22:44.545
He still gets photos printed out these days.

391
22:49.545 --> 22:51.025
What's this?

392
23:08.145 --> 23:09.545
What are you staring at?

393
23:09.625 --> 23:12.585
You've got something shady in the room,

394
23:12.665 --> 23:14.225
and it's making you look guilty?

395
23:14.985 --> 23:16.865
Would you stop talking nonsense?

396
23:16.945 --> 23:18.065
She's a young lady.

397
23:18.145 --> 23:21.705
She's waltzed right into your place. You've got so many young ladies,

398
23:21.785 --> 23:22.705
and I've said this about every one of them,

399
23:22.785 --> 23:24.785
but you defend her the most. You keep defending her like this.

400
23:24.865 --> 23:26.305
Believe it or not, I'll knock you out.

401
23:30.385 --> 23:32.465
It… It… It.. It's broken!

402
23:32.545 --> 23:33.545
Your laptop is fine.

403
23:33.625 --> 23:34.945
-It came loose. -It has a roll cage structure.

404
23:35.025 --> 23:35.905
It came loose from the impact.

405
23:38.985 --> 23:39.825
Wait.

406
23:40.865 --> 23:41.825
Wait.

407
23:43.145 --> 23:44.625
It isn't responding.

408
23:45.145 --> 23:46.225
What's wrong?

409
23:47.265 --> 23:48.865
Nothing. My hard drive…

410
23:48.945 --> 23:51.105
Well, it's not responding.

411
23:52.225 --> 23:53.105
-Hello, support service? -Oh my.

412
23:53.185 --> 23:54.945
Can you repair portable hard drives?

413
23:55.945 --> 23:57.425
-Oh no. -It won't work?

414
23:57.505 --> 23:59.545
This is bad. Yeah, it just fell.

415
23:59.625 --> 24:00.505
Mind if I have a go?

416
24:05.225 --> 24:07.705
Your laptop's USB ports are fine. The problem must be the hard drive.

417
24:09.345 --> 24:11.465
The support service can't fix it. Take it to a physical store.

418
24:12.825 --> 24:15.225
No, listen. I'm flying to Shenzhen tomorrow morning.

419
24:15.305 --> 24:17.425
All my roadshow materials are stored inside this drive.

420
24:17.505 --> 24:20.145
I'm running out of time. What am I going to do?

421
24:20.225 --> 24:21.065
Where's your backup?

422
24:22.825 --> 24:24.225
I didn't back this one up.

423
24:25.025 --> 24:26.665
If it's a port issue,

424
24:26.745 --> 24:29.225
swapping the drive's port might work.

425
24:29.305 --> 24:31.105
Or we could try data recovery.

426
24:31.185 --> 24:33.785
I've got all the tools back at my place.

427
24:33.865 --> 24:36.185
I could give it a go. Only a few hundred meters away.

428
24:37.225 --> 24:38.385
You know how to fix hard drives?

429
24:39.825 --> 24:41.185
You're saving my life, girl.

430
24:41.265 --> 24:43.185
Please help me. Thank you.

431
24:43.705 --> 24:45.385
-Wait for my update. -Thanks.

432
24:49.025 --> 24:52.745
You somehow found a girl who can repair hard drives.

433
24:52.825 --> 24:54.705
You really… You…

434
24:55.345 --> 24:56.585
Oh, no!

435
24:57.105 --> 24:58.145
What's wrong?

436
24:59.305 --> 25:02.585
All the material in there is bound by non-disclosure agreements.

437
25:02.665 --> 25:04.305
I… I do trust Xu Chi,

438
25:04.385 --> 25:06.425
but I think I need to keep an eye on her.

439
25:06.505 --> 25:07.665
-I'll go with you. -No,

440
25:08.905 --> 25:10.425
you'll go instead. You go instead.

441
25:11.145 --> 25:11.985
I don't know her well.

442
25:12.065 --> 25:14.025
But it's your portable hard drive. How should I…

443
25:14.105 --> 25:15.825
I'm in a panic. Stop stalling.

444
25:35.905 --> 25:36.745
Who's there?

445
25:40.705 --> 25:41.585
Well…

446
25:42.545 --> 25:45.385
Du said his hard drive

447
25:45.465 --> 25:46.385
seems

448
25:47.185 --> 25:48.385
to…

449
25:49.025 --> 25:50.465
He is worried about the material on it.

450
25:50.545 --> 25:52.385
-No… -This is my fault.

451
25:52.465 --> 25:54.105
I should've brought my tools over to your place.

452
25:54.185 --> 25:55.025
Well.

453
25:55.105 --> 25:57.225
-My bad. -No. Would you

454
25:57.945 --> 26:00.105
-like to come in? -Is it alright?

455
26:01.145 --> 26:03.145
Sure, it's just kind of messy.

456
26:06.145 --> 26:07.545
DELIVERIES PLEASE LEAVE AT DOOR TABLE ON THE LEFT

457
26:09.345 --> 26:11.705
I only have one chair at home, so you'll have to make do.

458
26:14.025 --> 26:16.225
I've swapped out the ports,

459
26:16.305 --> 26:18.265
but the laptop says it needs formatting.

460
26:18.345 --> 26:20.665
So I'm running DiskGenius now.

461
26:38.505 --> 26:40.545
Why do you even have these tools at home?

462
26:42.025 --> 26:45.265
My ex-boyfriend liked DIY, and I picked it up because it seemed fun.

463
26:46.225 --> 26:48.425
I planned to give this kit to him,

464
26:48.505 --> 26:50.065
but after we broke up, I ended up keeping it.

465
26:51.265 --> 26:52.265
FILE RECOVERY, DATA SCAN SEARCHING FOR FILES…

466
26:52.345 --> 26:53.425
Almost done.

467
26:53.505 --> 26:55.145
It's more than likely to be fine.

468
27:08.465 --> 27:11.705
I found it pretty amusing

469
27:11.785 --> 27:13.505
seeing how panicked Du was.

470
27:13.585 --> 27:14.745
You

471
27:15.905 --> 27:16.945
high-flying business elites

472
27:17.545 --> 27:19.945
are so used to working efficiently.

473
27:20.025 --> 27:21.705
Once one link in the chain breaks down,

474
27:21.785 --> 27:23.785
you're at a loss and come crashing off your pedestal.

475
27:23.865 --> 27:26.985
Yeah. You're right.

476
27:27.065 --> 27:28.385
But spare us some dignity, please.

477
27:28.465 --> 27:29.465
Alright.

478
27:30.065 --> 27:32.225
I promise I won't mention this to Du.

479
27:39.065 --> 27:39.905
It's fixed.

480
27:41.945 --> 27:42.785
Come here.

481
27:43.665 --> 27:44.945
Sit right here.

482
27:46.225 --> 27:47.145
-Right. -I…

483
27:47.225 --> 27:50.625
I'm copying his material onto another portable hard drive.

484
27:50.705 --> 27:52.665
Keep an eye on me

485
27:52.745 --> 27:55.585
and make sure I don't save any of his material onto my computer.

486
28:24.145 --> 28:25.345
PROGRESS: 94%

487
28:27.825 --> 28:30.025
Okay. Mission complete.

488
28:31.225 --> 28:32.225
What a relief.

489
28:33.105 --> 28:36.505
Remember to remind Du to get an SSD next time.

490
28:36.585 --> 28:37.905
They're much more shock-resistant.

491
28:37.985 --> 28:40.985
And always keep multiple backups for important data.

492
28:41.065 --> 28:42.385
I'm only an amateur.

493
28:42.465 --> 28:44.145
We just got lucky to fix it this time.

494
28:45.025 --> 28:46.905
No, it's not luck.

495
28:47.505 --> 28:49.905
You're naturally brilliant.

496
28:55.985 --> 28:59.265
Smooth talker. Then I won't charge you for the repair.

497
28:59.345 --> 29:01.145
Hurry back. Du must be anxious.

498
29:01.745 --> 29:02.825
-Go. -Thanks.

499
29:08.665 --> 29:09.625
Thank you.

500
29:25.105 --> 29:26.985
We've got it! Yes!

501
29:28.105 --> 29:28.985
Great! Perfect!

502
29:29.065 --> 29:31.025
This girl is incredible.

503
29:31.705 --> 29:34.025
Where did you find

504
29:34.105 --> 29:36.425
such an all-round talent?

505
29:38.225 --> 29:39.545
Back when we recruited interns.

506
29:39.625 --> 29:41.305
See what great taste I've got?

507
29:41.385 --> 29:43.745
Yeah, you're amazing. You're so great.

508
29:44.865 --> 29:46.545
Why didn't you ask her out?

509
29:46.625 --> 29:48.225
I want to take her out to dinner to thank her.

510
29:48.305 --> 29:49.745
She really bailed me out.

511
29:49.825 --> 29:50.945
She's one of us.

512
29:51.465 --> 29:52.665
There will be plenty of chances later.

513
29:53.385 --> 29:54.585
What do you mean "one of us"?

514
29:55.385 --> 29:56.825
I want her

515
29:57.345 --> 29:59.105
to take part in Wen Ruosen's project.

516
29:59.785 --> 30:02.145
Listen, watch how you talk to her from now on.

517
30:02.225 --> 30:04.385
I've got high hopes for her.

518
30:05.065 --> 30:07.065
Alright. You value her that much.

519
30:07.145 --> 30:07.985
What?

520
30:08.065 --> 30:10.265
Are you grooming her to be your right-hand?

521
30:13.345 --> 30:14.345
Maybe.

522
30:15.225 --> 30:16.225
You have no idea

523
30:16.745 --> 30:17.985
how fast she's improving.

524
30:19.065 --> 30:20.625
Just a few days ago,

525
30:20.705 --> 30:22.945
she was still weeping over her stolen project.

526
30:26.665 --> 30:27.905
Getting backstabbed

527
30:27.985 --> 30:29.825
by someone you trusted at work

528
30:30.345 --> 30:31.345
really hurts.

529
30:32.025 --> 30:33.465
You'll get used to it after a few times.

530
30:34.265 --> 30:37.105
Tomorrow when you go back to the office, don't overthink it.

531
30:37.185 --> 30:38.545
Just go head-to-head with her.

532
30:39.585 --> 30:41.945
After my little talk, she's completely transformed.

533
30:44.025 --> 30:46.105
She can calmly analyze the competitive landscape

534
30:46.185 --> 30:49.065
and skillfully handle interpersonal relationships.

535
30:49.585 --> 30:52.265
She's got the heiress wrapped around her finger.

536
30:53.025 --> 30:54.465
I was just at her place.

537
30:54.545 --> 30:57.465
Despite her cramped living space, she received me with total poise.

538
30:57.545 --> 31:00.505
I only have one chair at home, so you'll have to make do.

539
31:01.145 --> 31:03.305
She gives me that impression,

540
31:03.985 --> 31:05.505
she is neither insecure

541
31:06.145 --> 31:07.865
nor does her confidence seem overt.

542
31:08.905 --> 31:11.545
When I was her age, I was nowhere near as composed.

543
31:13.425 --> 31:14.945
That's really something.

544
31:15.865 --> 31:18.505
For a talent like this, you know, you need to hold onto her.

545
31:18.585 --> 31:20.785
Bring her straight over to C&amp;C.

546
31:20.865 --> 31:22.905
Train her personally yourself.

547
31:23.585 --> 31:26.505
Better than having her stuck at another company. Don't you think?

548
31:27.305 --> 31:28.305
No rush.

549
31:29.625 --> 31:32.145
Let her weather the storms at Maxmise first.

550
31:44.705 --> 31:45.545
Everyone,

551
31:46.145 --> 31:48.985
I just spoke with the people from Celestial Insurance.

552
31:49.505 --> 31:51.745
They aren't satisfied with our initial proposal.

553
31:52.785 --> 31:55.505
I don't see much point in pushing forward with it.

554
31:55.585 --> 31:57.225
We might as well

555
31:58.945 --> 31:59.865
scrap it and start over.

556
32:00.705 --> 32:02.105
Are you serious?

557
32:03.225 --> 32:04.945
We'll never get any sleep.

558
32:06.505 --> 32:09.345
Well, Ma Ke, the research report for Celestial Insurance is massive and messy.

559
32:09.425 --> 32:11.665
We're already burnt out. Are you sure we need to restart?

560
32:12.785 --> 32:15.505
Yang Rui, do you know who suggested this?

561
32:16.625 --> 32:17.825
Bu Tianna.

562
32:19.465 --> 32:22.305
Both she and Xu Chi are new hires. You seniors are already intimidated?

563
32:26.705 --> 32:27.825
Alright.

564
32:27.905 --> 32:29.385
Let's hear what they both have to say.

565
32:30.185 --> 32:31.265
I love competition

566
32:32.065 --> 32:34.345
because I have never lost.

567
32:35.265 --> 32:36.745
What a coincidence. Neither have I.

568
32:36.825 --> 32:37.825
Alright.

569
32:38.345 --> 32:40.545
So, everyone in agreement?

570
33:04.745 --> 33:07.305
Their team's consultants drafted new proposals,

571
33:07.385 --> 33:08.385
but in the end,

572
33:08.465 --> 33:10.905
Bu Tianna and Xu Chi clashed the most fiercely.

573
33:11.425 --> 33:13.545
What approaches did each of them take?

574
33:13.625 --> 33:15.505
Bu Tianna took the top-down approach.

575
33:15.585 --> 33:18.265
She kept meeting senior executives from major insurance firms.

576
33:18.345 --> 33:20.065
She knows plenty of high-ranking contacts.

577
33:20.145 --> 33:23.105
She also knows a great deal about Celestial Insurance's competitors.

578
33:23.785 --> 33:26.385
Standing on giants' shoulders, naturally, she sees further.

579
33:26.465 --> 33:28.105
Xu Chi built grassroots connections instead.

580
33:28.185 --> 33:29.985
She spent lots of time with Celestial Insurance's staff,

581
33:30.065 --> 33:33.025
trying to figure out exactly why the previous proposal got rejected.

582
33:33.985 --> 33:35.185
So who do you fancy more?

583
33:36.305 --> 33:37.225
Bu Tianna.

584
33:42.025 --> 33:44.025
You're rooting for Xu Chi, aren't you?

585
33:45.665 --> 33:46.905
I suppose I am.

586
33:46.985 --> 33:48.345
Bu Tianna's got connections,

587
33:48.865 --> 33:50.385
but Xu Chi has solid backing too.

588
33:55.345 --> 33:56.305
Backing?

589
33:56.905 --> 33:58.265
Do you spot something off?

590
33:59.305 --> 34:00.625
It might be

591
34:01.745 --> 34:02.945
an issue with the India branch.

592
34:03.025 --> 34:05.145
-The India branch? -Right.

593
34:07.185 --> 34:09.304
Celestial Insurance doesn't have an overseas branch in India.

594
34:10.744 --> 34:13.105
It's not your mistake. It's mine.

595
34:14.264 --> 34:16.744
Our company recently brought on an Indian partner.

596
34:17.264 --> 34:18.744
My frequent meetings with him

597
34:19.824 --> 34:20.985
are impacting me.

598
34:21.585 --> 34:23.744
I've confused a nod with a "no",

599
34:24.665 --> 34:25.905
and a shake with a "yes".

600
34:34.865 --> 34:36.145
Are you messing with me on purpose?

601
34:38.065 --> 34:39.784
Alright. Back to business.

602
34:39.865 --> 34:42.185
As competitors,

603
34:42.264 --> 34:44.425
I'm not in a position to comment on Maxmise's project.

604
34:45.145 --> 34:48.344
But in the slides you sent me, all key information has been redacted.

605
34:48.425 --> 34:49.385
That's well done.

606
34:49.985 --> 34:52.304
From now on, for our private conversations,

607
34:52.385 --> 34:54.505
we'll only discuss ideas, no concrete details.

608
34:55.105 --> 34:57.825
Otherwise, we risk leaking confidential business information.

609
34:57.905 --> 34:58.865
Got it.

610
34:58.945 --> 35:01.105
Overall, this proposal you showed me is logically well-structured.

611
35:01.185 --> 35:03.465
As an analyst's first draft,

612
35:03.545 --> 35:04.505
it's pretty solid.

613
35:06.425 --> 35:09.825
Only pretty solid as an analyst's draft?

614
35:10.865 --> 35:11.825
What more do you expect?

615
35:11.905 --> 35:14.905
Experience comes from repeated failures.

616
35:15.665 --> 35:17.585
You've been on this project for barely over a month.

617
35:17.665 --> 35:20.145
Do you really expect a flawless finished proposal right now?

618
35:22.025 --> 35:24.865
Still, you can compete against Bu Tianna with this,

619
35:24.945 --> 35:25.825
and you'll stand a fighting chance.

620
35:27.545 --> 35:30.225
But my goal isn't just to beat her in this competition.

621
35:30.745 --> 35:32.865
I want the client's genuine approval of my solution.

622
35:33.545 --> 35:36.065
Client satisfaction is a relative notion.

623
35:36.145 --> 35:38.625
Getting them to compromise and buy in is what usually happens.

624
35:39.225 --> 35:40.545
But I--

625
35:41.185 --> 35:43.025
XIAOXI

626
35:45.305 --> 35:47.025
ANSWER

627
35:47.105 --> 35:48.985
Xinzhi, I'll arrive in Beijing the day after tomorrow.

628
35:49.065 --> 35:51.225
-In the evening-- -Ms. Liu, hold on a second.

629
35:54.545 --> 35:55.465
Just a moment.

630
35:55.985 --> 35:57.665
Chi, do your research thoroughly.

631
35:57.745 --> 35:58.905
The client will respond to it.

632
36:00.705 --> 36:01.545
Okay.

633
36:37.305 --> 36:38.425
Xu Chi,

634
36:39.025 --> 36:41.185
you spent the day on site for the project.

635
36:41.265 --> 36:42.585
Why are you back at the office?

636
36:43.505 --> 36:45.545
Something's still off about this proposal,

637
36:45.625 --> 36:47.985
so I came back to look up materials,

638
36:48.065 --> 36:49.425
hoping for some inspiration.

639
36:52.065 --> 36:54.705
Alright. I've got a little spare time. I'll take a look for you.

640
36:54.785 --> 36:56.345
-Great. -Come on. Walk me through your thinking.

641
36:56.425 --> 36:57.425
Okay.

642
37:00.385 --> 37:03.785
My new proposal focuses on breaking down Celestial Insurance's value tree.

643
37:23.905 --> 37:26.705
Xu Chi, this proposal is far too complicated.

644
37:27.865 --> 37:30.825
I'd suggest redoing it with a focus

645
37:30.905 --> 37:32.905
on scenario-based big data business and enhancing the customer experience.

646
37:34.065 --> 37:35.025
Redo it?

647
37:35.105 --> 37:36.665
But won't that get too granular?

648
37:36.745 --> 37:40.185
Besides, I barely have experience with scenario-based design.

649
37:41.305 --> 37:43.825
Our last proposal got rejected because it was too abstract.

650
37:45.985 --> 37:46.865
I believe in you.

651
37:47.625 --> 37:49.585
Alright. Don't stay up too late.

652
37:49.665 --> 37:50.665
Get some rest.

653
37:55.025 --> 37:56.425
Redo it…

654
38:05.225 --> 38:06.065
Didn't get much sleep?

655
38:07.145 --> 38:08.865
Ma Ke suddenly asked me to refocus

656
38:08.945 --> 38:10.785
on scenario-based big data business the day before yesterday.

657
38:11.465 --> 38:13.105
You should have told me earlier, so I could've helped revise it.

658
38:14.665 --> 38:15.745
Good work, everyone.

659
38:15.825 --> 38:18.145
Today's weekly meeting is to go over progress

660
38:18.225 --> 38:20.185
and requirements for each of your projects.

661
38:20.265 --> 38:21.345
Let's begin.

662
38:22.425 --> 38:23.745
-Ma Ke. -Everyone's here.

663
38:24.265 --> 38:26.305
-Mr. Pi, you're back. -Just got back from the US.

664
38:26.825 --> 38:29.425
I was heading to my office to beat jet lag,

665
38:30.025 --> 38:31.305
but seeing you having your weekly meeting,

666
38:31.385 --> 38:32.985
I wanted to drop in and listen.

667
38:33.065 --> 38:35.265
Carry on. Don't mind me. Thank you.

668
38:38.065 --> 38:39.065
Take a seat.

669
38:44.185 --> 38:45.505
What's wrong?

670
38:46.865 --> 38:48.105
Why so serious?

671
38:50.025 --> 38:52.385
I have a question. Ma Ke,

672
38:52.985 --> 38:54.425
is this ongoing project

673
38:54.505 --> 38:55.985
hitting roadblocks?

674
38:58.665 --> 39:00.385
We've finished research and framework building.

675
39:00.465 --> 39:01.705
The client is happy with that part.

676
39:01.785 --> 39:03.705
But they want revisions to the proposal.

677
39:03.785 --> 39:06.105
We're updating it right now.

678
39:07.785 --> 39:09.105
I read the first version.

679
39:10.105 --> 39:12.745
Do you have a new draft ready?

680
39:13.665 --> 39:15.105
We now have five proposals,

681
39:15.185 --> 39:16.945
each taking a different approach.

682
39:17.625 --> 39:19.425
Mr. Pi, since you're here,

683
39:19.505 --> 39:21.065
-shall we walk you through them? -Alright.

684
39:26.425 --> 39:30.145
Xu Chi, you're in charge of scenario-based big data business, right?

685
39:31.105 --> 39:31.945
Right.

686
39:33.425 --> 39:35.745
Mr. Pi, Xu Chi has been telling me

687
39:35.825 --> 39:37.505
she's very confident in her proposal.

688
39:37.585 --> 39:38.705
Let her go first.

689
39:41.185 --> 39:42.865
-Wait, a couple of days ago, I just… -Xu Chi,

690
39:42.945 --> 39:45.225
if you've got solid ideas, speak up.

691
39:45.305 --> 39:46.945
Let Mr. Pi give us his feedback.

692
39:47.745 --> 39:49.545
Ma Ke is right. Xu Chi,

693
39:50.065 --> 39:53.665
you were brimming with confidence on the Bolo Culture project last time.

694
39:53.745 --> 39:54.585
Tell us your thoughts.

695
39:58.385 --> 39:59.985
I'll give a brief overview.

696
40:30.705 --> 40:31.785
Xu Chi, hold on.

697
40:33.305 --> 40:34.745
I have a question.

698
40:35.345 --> 40:36.825
For the scenario-based customization

699
40:36.905 --> 40:38.585
of pet medical insurance you mentioned,

700
40:39.105 --> 40:40.945
what's the annual premium revenue for each one?

701
40:43.105 --> 40:44.665
Sorry.

702
40:47.305 --> 40:48.905
Roughly over 100 million a year.

703
40:54.185 --> 40:56.185
Huayuan Insurance is comparable in size

704
40:56.265 --> 40:57.425
to Celestial Insurance.

705
40:57.505 --> 41:01.985
Their pet medical insurance premium was around 50 million last year.

706
41:02.065 --> 41:03.905
Celestial Insurance's annual premium revenue

707
41:03.985 --> 41:05.025
is nearly 100 billion.

708
41:05.865 --> 41:08.905
The pet medical insurance scenario you proposed

709
41:09.505 --> 41:12.265
can only generate at most several billion in premiums.

710
41:12.345 --> 41:15.265
What impact could that possibly have on Celestial Insurance's

711
41:15.945 --> 41:16.785
multi-billion-yuan business?

712
41:17.905 --> 41:20.105
I haven't collected enough materials.

713
41:20.185 --> 41:21.545
In this case,

714
41:22.185 --> 41:23.585
why did you tell Ma Ke

715
41:24.385 --> 41:25.945
you were confident in your proposal?

716
41:30.145 --> 41:31.425
Ma Ke,

717
41:32.065 --> 41:34.265
as the project manager, what's your take?

718
41:34.985 --> 41:36.025
Alright.

719
41:46.625 --> 41:48.105
Mr. Pi.

720
41:48.185 --> 41:49.025
My approach starts

721
41:49.105 --> 41:51.105
with the key value drivers of their current business.

722
41:51.705 --> 41:54.185
I built a value tree for Celestial Insurance.

723
41:54.265 --> 41:55.025
Please take a look.
